lab 8 - when does postgres use the index?

table: 1,000,000 rows, orders(id, customer_id, created_at, total).

- WHERE customer_id = 42 (about 20 rows): index scan, 0.08 ms.
- WHERE created_at > now() - interval '1 day' (0.3% of rows): bitmap heap scan, 4 ms.
- WHERE total > 10 (95% of rows): seq scan, 110 ms. forcing the index (enable_seqscan=off) made it 380 ms. the planner was right.
- after deleting 40% of rows without vacuum the seq scan got slower (dead tuples still read). VACUUM fixed it.

conclusion: selectivity decides. an index is not always faster.
